el was going to have  its work cut out for it fortunately for  film goers everywhere director james  cameron managed to expand the scale  while maintaining the intimate terror of  what came before the results is aliens  an action-packed masterpiece as beloved  as its predecessor set 57 years after  her initial encounter with a xenomorph  the film finds alan ripley awakened from  hypersleep just in time to assist the  military expedition to the now colonized  lv-426 yes it's the same place where the  deadly species was first discovered  despite traveling with a crew of  hardened marines it doesn't take long  for the creatures to begin taking them  down one by one their advance to  weaponry fails to protect them for long  and soon only a handful are left alive  in a last-ditch attempt to rescue young  newt the colony's only living survivor  ripley goes head-to-head with the  xenomorph queen who is none too thrilled  to have her babies set on fire their  grudge match eventually results in the  queen being blown out of their ship's  airlock and suddenly all seems right  with the world the planet has been  destroyed the aliens are all dead and  ripley even has a new surrogate daughter  the final moments of the film seem  almost hopeful for the future  that is as long as you ignore the rest  of the franchise i'm sorry newt  you don't have to be sorry it wasn't  your fault the collection a 2012 c  quarter 2009's the collector comes from  patrick melton and marcus dunstan who  wrote the feast trilogy and four of the  sore films it's no surprise that the  first film is a grizzly stomach churning  affair involving elaborate booby traps  and insidious torture methods it follows  a mysterious figure who kidnaps his  victims for nefarious purposes the film  ends with him abducting a man named  arkian who is inadvertently released at  the beginning of the sequel this time  around we get a look at the maniacs  hideout an intricate warehouse filled  with all manner of spikes and so